ing movies  and surfing the web and that's mainly  what I ended up using it for even though  the CPU is weak that doesn't really  hinder it for these tasks browsing is  really smooth and the sharp bright  display is great to look at the 16 by 10  ratio compared to 4 by 3 means that  black bars are kept to a minimum when  standard content is viewed and the quad  speakers are shockingly loud while it  doesn't sound as good as the new iPad  pros it's definitely still great and is  actually louder in the iPad air can't  even compete  [Music]  being an oled screen the contrast ratio  is awesome and unlike the iPads even the  pro youtube will let you stream in 1440p  which maximizes the display and gives  you such a nice looking image all of  that coupled with a cheap expandable  storage for downloads makes this  experience so good that I think it's  probably the best tablet for watching  videos if you want to get a little bit  of work done Samsung does tell a $130  keyboard accessory but it's kind of  mediocre I typed for at least an hour  and even though I got used to it it's  still hard to use if only Samsung made  the keys slightly wider that would have  made for a much better experience Apple  charges more for their keyboards but the  quality is better with more  adjustability and the typing experience  is on another level a secret weapon of  the s5 EE is Dex a PC like interface  that can now be used without a display  this is great if you want to be very  flexible with multitasking and unlike  the iPads you can use a mouse which is  fantastic plugging into a larger display  and a better Bluetooth keyboard really  makes us a workhorse for research and  typing but I think there's not really  that many that will utilize this of  course with a Android you can organize  your files however you'd like and  archive them too unlike Apple's lockdown  iOS it really is a shame that so many  Android apps aren't optimized for  tablets some wouldn't let me use their  keyboards while others wouldn't even go  into landscape mode and honestly I don't  know if this will ever change since the  Android tablet market share is so low  developers aren't really incentivized to  update their apps this brings me to my  main question in a world of iPads does  the s5 e have room to compete yes I  think so but the slot is very small if  you're someone that wants a tablet for  watching videos surfing the web the s5 e  is absolutely fantastic  but even then I wish Samsung spent a  little more money on the processor to  make it smoother and more future-proof  but for almost everyone else whether you  want to get some work done you want to  type you want a game I would say you  should wait for the S type if you want  Android or if you want to just go with  the flow go and buy an iPad like almost  everybody else does and you'll have  access to a ton of great apps a great  screen and great performance thank you  guys for watching click the circle above  if you want to subscribe to see more  videos like this one and also that  little notification Bell check out our  s5 e vs iPad air compares  and gaming videos right over here this  been max max sec and I'll see you in the  next one
 

